plum:
From hand to hand they pushed the wine,
They sucked the pulp of plum and peach;
They sang, they jested, and they laughed,

plucked:
Heap my golden plates with fruit,
Golden fruit, fresh-plucked and ripe;
Strike the bells and breathe the pipe;

plums:
'Have done with sorrow;
I'll bring you plums to-morrow
Fresh on their mother twigs,

plumb:
Set each sharp-edged, fire-bitten brick
Straight by the plumb-line's shivering length;
Make my marvelous wall so thick

pluggin:
Some bright day you 'll wake up there,--
Keep a-pluggin' away.
Perseverance still is king;

plumed:
The grave cow heavy-laden:
I've seen grand ladies plumed and silked,
But not a sweeter maiden;

plumper:
The nuts are getting brown;
The berry's cheek is plumper,
The rose is out of town.

plus:
Comme l'amour, comme la mort;
Et j'ai fait les plus belles de belle argile
Sèche et fragile.
